true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"exec-53c90309-f673-46bd-81f8-5bcedf9cbd22","name":"rtk rg -n -A 5 -B 5 'percent\\(|incrementalIncomeVsSimpleEarn|首次|无法精确计算|PhaseOneAssessment\\(' src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest.java","raw_input":"{\"command\":\"rtk rg -n -A 5 -B 5 'percent\\\\(|incrementalIncomeVsSimpleEarn|首次|无法精确计算|PhaseOneAssessment\\\\(' src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest.java\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree\"}","input":{"command":"rtk rg -n -A 5 -B 5 'percent\\(|incrementalIncomeVsSimpleEarn|首次|无法精确计算|PhaseOneAssessment\\(' src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest.java src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest.java","cwd":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"Thinking":{"text":"**Defining precision fixes****我正校准精度回归用例****我正补齐回归边界**","signature":null}},{"Text":"{\n \"schema_version\":1,\n \"workstream_id\": \"ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\",\n \"run_id\": \"run-1793029770286\",\n \"node_id\": \"design.codex_arch_review\",\n \"result\": {\n \"artifact_type\": \"agent_output_contract\",\n \"decision\": \"NEEDS_REVISION\",\n \"summary\": \"六文件方案的计算口径与职责划分合理，但精度断言和展示舍入不影响建议的验证设计尚未满足合同。\",\n \"lifecycle_status\": \"READY\",\n \"blocking\": true,\n \"checks\": [\n \"已先审阅 Review Evidence Brief，再核对完整设计及六项 Declared Planned Files；针对精度与建议边界定向核验原始合同、服务及 CLI代码。\",\n \"范围审查通过：服务计算、record 承载、CLI 展示、两份测试和一份说明覆盖所需职责；当前 GOAL 文件清单属于提案，不代表 EXECUTION 写入授权。\",\n \"公式审查通过：复用 simpleEarnIncome 和 knownTotal，以对冲空头名义金额为分母，不重复计费、不年化、不按结算间隔换算；独立样例的180、0.02 和 -10/0/10 均成立。\",\n \"边界审查：WARN。权威派生结果由 PhaseOneAssessmentService负责，PhaseOneAssessment 承载，CLI只消费；本次不新增持久实例或执行状态，也不迁移既有事实来源。\",\n \"端到端不变量审查：Declared by 为 AC-1 至 AC-4；Consumed by 为 CLI；Enforced before 为服务在产生数值前检查 blockers/unknowns；Failure route 为 Optional.empty 加既有原因；Proven by 尚为拟议测试，精度与舍入隔离的 Cannot-bypass test 存在下述缺口。\",\n \"生命周期审查：正常完成和证据不足分支均已覆盖设计；未引入共享可变状态、索引、锁、事务、队列、缓存或外部写入，因此并发、超时、崩溃、重启、回滚和补偿无需新增机制。但计算结果到 CLI 的防绕过验证仍适用，不能一并声明不适用。\",\n \"未发现需要增加平台、兼容机制或扩大六文件范围的理由；修订应仅加强现有测试设计和边界说明。\"\n ],\n \"evidence\": [\n \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/artifacts/contracts/node-contract-compile-007/task-contract.md：AC-1 要求 DECIMAL128；TR-1 要求断言基于 BigDecimal 原值；AC-2 禁止用 CLI 舍入值重新决定建议。\",\n \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793027503466/outputs/design-claude.contract.json：除不尽场景明确计划在 setScale(6, HALF_UP) 后断言，示例为0.066667；CLI 测试主要检查标签与六位小数格式。\",\n \"src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java：当前以完整精度 delta.signum() 决定建议，仅在 blockers 和 unknowns 均为空时提供净收入及增量。\",\n \"src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java:301：money() 按两位小数展示；:305 的 percent()乘以100 后按六位小数展示。这些展示结果可能掩盖正负微小增量。\"\n ],\n \"missing_evidence\": [],\n \"must_fix\": [\n \"R1（AC-1、AC-2、TR-1）：修改除不尽场景的测试设计，直接断言 record 中 BigDecimal 原值符合独立确定的 DECIMAL128预期，不先 setScale(6)。当前断言会让服务提前舍入为0.066667 的错误实现通过，无法守住设计承诺的计算精度。六位展示断言应留在 CLI 测试；文档将“未舍入原值”准确表述为“按 DECIMAL128计算、未按展示精度进一步舍入的值”。\",\n \"R2（AC-2、AC-4）：补充展示舍入不能改变建议的具体测试，并修正“防绕过边界不适用”的声明。可在 AC-2 参数下使用累计费率0.0199999999 和0.0200000001：两者百分比均显示为2.000000%，原始增量却分别为 -0.000001 和0.000001，必须保留不同的既有建议及相应首次验证上限语义。同时将独立样例的 CLI断言固定为阈值2.000000%，不能仅匹配任意六位小数百分比。上述补充均可落在已声明的两份测试文件内。\"\n ],\n \"contract_obligations\": [],\n \"acceptance_notes\": [\n \"证据不足时返回空值并沿用既有 blockers/unknowns 的方案可接受；历史区间完整性限制继续保留，不要求新增历史完整性判定机制。\",\n \"本次是设计审查，未实现代码、未执行测试，不将未来测试计划描述为已验证或已闭环。\",\n \"完整回归、程序化测试报告、独立验收、交付批准、精确候选应用、人工或明确委派的 commit 和原 finalize仍属于后续交付要求；本次审查不替代这些步骤。\"\n ],\n \"open_risks\": [],\n \"changed_files\": [],\n \"verification_summary\": \"已完成合同与完整设计审查，并通过只读工具核验关键代码；发现两项测试设计阻断，未修改任何文件，未运行测试。\",\n \"failure\": {\n \"category_hint\": \"设计验证不足\",\n \"verification_remediation\": \"NONE\",\n \"contract_gaps\": [\n \"除不尽场景的断言未守住 TR-1 所要求的 BigDecimal 原值精度。\",\n \"缺少 AC-2 所要求的展示舍入不影响建议的针对性验证。\"\n ],\n \"out_of_scope_files\": [],\n \"missing_tests\": [\n \"直接验证 DECIMAL128 原值的除不尽场景。\",\n \"展示费率相同但原始增量异号时，建议和首次验证上限保持原语义的场景。\",\n \"独立样例阈值精确展示为2.000000% 的断言。\"\n ],\n \"context_gaps\": [],\n \"reason\": \"当前测试方案可能放过服务提前舍入或建议依赖展示值的错误实现，需要在进入实现前补全验证设计。\"\n },\n \"reread_reasons\": []\n }\n}"}],"tool_results":{"exec-b998518d-94d3-4f01-b928-ed53d3a6f7c4":{"tool_use_id":"exec-b998518d-94d3-4f01-b928-ed53d3a6f7c4","tool_name":"rtk read /Users/kriswang/.codex/skills/boundary-first-engineering/SKILL.md","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"---\\nname: boundary-first-engineering\\ndescription: Use before changing or reviewing systems with non-trivial state, lifecycle transitions, workflow/orchestration, external adapters, retries, recovery, compensation, async workers, queues, schedulers, human decisions, structured contracts, events, ledgers, projections, dashboards, reports, UI/CLI/API status, or completion semantics. Trigger when symptoms include repeated local fixes, ambiguous completion, stale running state, duplicated status logic, natural-language parsing drift, hidden evidence, projection disagreement, retry/resume confusion, terminal-state leaks, or any temptation to fix a state bug with handler-local if/else.\\n---\\n\\n# Boundary-First Engineering\\n\\nUse this skill as a state-boundary discipline, not as a project-specific checklist. The goal is to prevent local patches from bypassing domain boundaries.\\n\\n## First Move\\n\\nBefore editing code, state the suspected boundary:\\n\\n- Domain state / lifecycle model\\n- Definition / instance / execution model\\n- External adapter / activity boundary\\n- Structured artifact / event / command contract\\n- Retry / recovery / compensation semantics\\n- Human decision / approval semantics\\n- Completion / terminal-state contract\\n- Projection / UI / CLI / API / report read model\\n\\nIf the boundary is unclear, inspect the model, source of truth, and data flow first. Do not start with DOM tweaks, substring rules, handler-local branches, or projection fixes.\\n\\n\\n## Automatic Boundary Loop\\n\\nFor any boundary-sensitive task, run this loop until the material boundary findings are resolved or explicitly accepted as debt:\\n\\n```text\\nAnalyze -> Modify -> Review -> Reflect -> Analyze\\n```\\n\\n- Analyze: name the boundary, source of truth, affected projections, and expected invariant before editing.\\n- Modify: change the source-of-truth model or typed boundary first; update projections after.\\n- Review: re-run this skill against the diff and classify findings as PASS / WARN / FAIL.\\n- Reflect: record why the issue happened, whether the model/discipline missed a trigger, and what test or rule prevents recurrence.\\n- Re-enter Analyze when Review is WARN/FAIL, when a fix introduces a new boundary, or when the reasoning relied on a stopgap.\\n\\nDo not treat a stateful fix as complete after one green test if the Review or Reflect step exposes an unguarded boundary.\\n\\n## Model Ownership Check\\n\\nReplay the existing model before proposing or editing stateful code:\\n\\n```text\\nExisting model:\\n- Definition: what is declared or configured?\\n- Instance: what durable business/process occurrence exists?\\n- Execution: what concrete run/attempt/process happened?\\n- Event / Ledger / History: what facts are recorded and replayable?\\n- Artifact / Contract: what structured output is trusted?\\n- Human Decision: what did a person decide, and at which gate?\\n- Projection: what is read-only display or reporting?\\n\\nProblem ownership:\\n- Which existing object should own this fact or transition?\\n\\nNew concept needed:\\n- No / Yes. If yes, why can no existing object carry it?\\n```\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n- Prefer established domain terms. Do not invent synonyms such as attempt, run, job, task, stage, or checkpoint if definition / instance / execution / event / artifact / gate already fits.\\n- Execution owns runtime facts: pid, command, stdout, stderr, exit code, timeout, interruption, stale process, retry evidence, and external tool failures.\\n- Instance owns the durable occurrence of a process, node, order, job, request, workflow, or business lifecycle.\\n- Iteration or revision owns semantic rework. Runtime retry is not semantic iteration.\\n- Goal or business aggregate owns user intent and satisfaction truth. Workflow completion alone is not goal satisfaction.\\n- Projection owns display only. UI, CLI, dashboards, summaries, and reports must not invent state.\\n\\n## Source Of Truth\\n\\nIdentify one authoritative source before changing behavior:\\n\\n-..."},"output":{"formatted_output":"---\nname: boundary-first-engineering\ndescription: Use before changing or reviewing systems with non-trivial state, lifecycle transitions, workflow/orchestration, external adapters, retries, recovery, compensation, async workers, queues, schedulers, human decisions, structured contracts, events, ledgers, projections, dashboards, reports, UI/CLI/API status, or completion semantics. Trigger when symptoms include repeated local fixes, ambiguous completion, stale running state, duplicated status logic, natural-language parsing drift, hidden evidence, projection disagreement, retry/resume confusion, terminal-state leaks, or any temptation to fix a state bug with handler-local if/else.\n---\n\n# Boundary-First Engineering\n\nUse this skill as a state-boundary discipline, not as a project-specific checklist. The goal is to prevent local patches from bypassing domain boundaries.\n\n## First Move\n\nBefore editing code, state the suspected boundary:\n\n- Domain state / lifecycle model\n- Definition / instance / execution model\n- External adapter / activity boundary\n- Structured artifact / event / command contract\n- Retry / recovery / compensation semantics\n- Human decision / approval semantics\n- Completion / terminal-state contract\n- Projection / UI / CLI / API / report read model\n\nIf the boundary is unclear, inspect the model, source of truth, and data flow first. Do not start with DOM tweaks, substring rules, handler-local branches, or projection fixes.\n\n\n## Automatic Boundary Loop\n\nFor any boundary-sensitive task, run this loop until the material boundary findings are resolved or explicitly accepted as debt:\n\n```text\nAnalyze -> Modify -> Review -> Reflect -> Analyze\n```\n\n- Analyze: name the boundary, source of truth, affected projections, and expected invariant before editing.\n- Modify: change the source-of-truth model or typed boundary first; update projections after.\n- Review: re-run this skill against the diff and classify findings as PASS / WARN / FAIL.\n- Reflect: record why the issue happened, whether the model/discipline missed a trigger, and what test or rule prevents recurrence.\n- Re-enter Analyze when Review is WARN/FAIL, when a fix introduces a new boundary, or when the reasoning relied on a stopgap.\n\nDo not treat a stateful fix as complete after one green test if the Review or Reflect step exposes an unguarded boundary.\n\n## Model Ownership Check\n\nReplay the existing model before proposing or editing stateful code:\n\n```text\nExisting model:\n- Definition: what is declared or configured?\n- Instance: what durable business/process occurrence exists?\n- Execution: what concrete run/attempt/process happened?\n- Event / Ledger / History: what facts are recorded and replayable?\n- Artifact / Contract: what structured output is trusted?\n- Human Decision: what did a person decide, and at which gate?\n- Projection: what is read-only display or reporting?\n\nProblem ownership:\n- Which existing object should own this fact or transition?\n\nNew concept needed:\n- No / Yes. If yes, why can no existing object carry it?\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Prefer established domain terms. Do not invent synonyms such as attempt, run, job, task, stage, or checkpoint if definition / instance / execution / event / artifact / gate already fits.\n- Execution owns runtime facts: pid, command, stdout, stderr, exit code, timeout, interruption, stale process, retry evidence, and external tool failures.\n- Instance owns the durable occurrence of a process, node, order, job, request, workflow, or business lifecycle.\n- Iteration or revision owns semantic rework. Runtime retry is not semantic iteration.\n- Goal or business aggregate owns user intent and satisfaction truth. Workflow completion alone is not goal satisfaction.\n- Projection owns display only. UI, CLI, dashboards, summaries, and reports must not invent state.\n\n## Source Of Truth\n\nIdentify one authoritative source before changing behavior:\n\n- Domain object or aggregate for business truth.\n- Event history / ledger for how the state was reached.\n- Structured artifact / schema for LLM or external output.\n- Adapter metadata for external runtime failures.\n- Read model only for projection.\n\nIf the same status, next action, or decision is computed in UI, CLI, API, and runtime separately, stop and centralize it behind a semantic read model.\n\n## Sibling Boundary Sweep\n\nWhen a fix removes or relocates a source of truth, do not stop at the first failing symbol or the first user-mentioned method. Search for sibling concepts that share the same boundary.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Removing one workflow variant generated by Java means checking every built-in variant, not only the one named in the bug.\n- Moving one lifecycle definition to JSON means checking all lifecycle definition sources, docs, tests, CLI options, smoke cases, and generated examples.\n- Centralizing one projection field means checking every UI / CLI / API / report surface that answers the same user question.\n\nRequired sweep before completion:\n\n```text\nPrimary concept changed:\nSibling concepts with the same owner:\nAuthoritative source after the change:\nOld source paths removed:\nTests that protect the new boundary:\nResidual compatibility kept:\nWhy the residual compatibility is necessary:\n```\n\nIf residual compatibility is not necessary, delete it. If it is kept, document the owner, expiry condition, and test coverage. Do not keep a legacy path just because it still passes.\n\n## Definition / Registry Drift Sweep\n\nWhen a system has declarative definitions plus code registries, treat drift as a boundary risk, not a simple missing entry.\n\nCheck these pairs together:\n\n- Workflow / lifecycle definition vs runtime factory or handler registry.\n- Node ids and edge outcomes vs artifact/output contract registry.\n- Failure reason catalog vs recovery assessment and operator next actions.\n- Gate metadata / allowed actions vs CLI, API, UI, and autorun actions.\n- Read model / projection semantics vs UI, CLI, API, reports, and dashboards.\n\nRules:\n\n- A registry is acceptable only as a named boundary: capability catalog, failure signal catalog, contract validator, or projection policy.\n- A registry is not acceptable when it silently becomes a second workflow definition or a second state machine.\n- When adding or fixing one registry entry, add a consistency test against the authoritative definition.\n- Do not preserve old registry paths unless real users need compatibility; if kept, state the owner and expiry condition.\n- If declarative config and code disagree, fix the source-of-truth boundary first, then update projections.\n\nRequired drift check:\n\n```text\nAuthoritative definition:\nCode registry/catalog touching the same concept:\nCan the registry derive from the definition?\nConsistency test added:\nResidual hardcode kept:\nWhy the hardcode is a named boundary rather than drift:\n```\n\n## External Adapter Rule\n\nTreat LLMs, CLIs, network APIs, databases, queues, file I/O, and tools as external activities/adapters:\n\n- Record their inputs, outputs, exit status, duration, and failure category.\n- Do not let natural-language text directly mutate domain state.\n- Convert external output into a typed artifact, event, or failure signal first.\n- Classify adapter failures separately from business rejection.\n- Keep provider-specific wording in an adapter catalog or parser, not in workflow or UI code.\n\n## Transition And Terminal Rules\n\n- Core runtime must guard terminal states before creating new execution records or side effects.\n- Terminal states may allow observation, summary, export, or audit; they must not allow run/resume/retry/approve unless the domain explicitly defines a reopening command.\n- Guards must be side-effect free. Actions that mutate state belong in transition handlers or domain methods.\n- Retry handles recoverable execution failure. Repair handles unmet business goal. Compensation closes or offsets an already-taken wrong action. Do not mix them.\n- If an error is terminal/non-retriable, model it explicitly instead of hiding it behind a catch-all retry.\n\n## Human Decision Rules\n\n- Human gates must expose allowed actions, evidence, recommendation, and consequences.\n- Current gates may expose actions. Historical gates are read-only evidence.\n- Human review should judge product/domain evidence, not compensate for unclear workflow mechanics.\n- Gate purpose should come from metadata or domain model. Node-id fallback is acceptable only as isolated legacy compatibility.\n\n## Projection Rules\n\n- Define the user question first: where is it, why did it stop, what evidence supports this, what action is allowed next, or what happened historically?\n- Put object-specific evidence before shared context.\n- Current-state panels and historical evidence panels must be different modes.\n- If multiple cards/items look identical, the projection is wrong even if the data is technically present.\n- UI, CLI, API, reports, and dashboards should consume the same read model for status, attention, next action, and completion.\n\n## Red Flags\n\nPause and redo the ownership check when you see:\n\n- A fix that is mostly another contains/startsWith branch.\n- A source-of-truth migration that fixes one variant, mode, command, or projection while leaving siblings on the old mechanism.\n- A terminal object that can still be resumed or approved.\n- Runtime failure recorded as business failure.\n- Semantic repair recorded as runtime retry.\n- Natural-language parsing used as the primary decision source.\n- UI says one status while CLI/API/ledger says another.\n- Projection code scanning files and deriving lifecycle decisions independently.\n- Human review needed to validate flow mechanics rather than domain evidence.\n- A new field added to one surface but not to the authoritative model.\n- A registry or factory that repeats workflow nodes, edge outcomes, handler types, or output contracts without a consistency test.\n- A real-case failure that is fixed by adding one more string branch without sweeping sibling reasons, states, projections, and registries.\n\n## Stopgap Admission\n\nUse a stopgap only when the system is blocked and a model fix is too costly right now. Label it explicitly:\n\n```text\nStopgap fix:\n- What is contained:\n- Why this is not the final model:\n- Why it does not corrupt the source of truth:\n- Follow-up model fix:\n- Revisit trigger:\n```\n\nDo not call a stopgap a lifecycle closure.\n\n## Required Review Output\n\nFor design or review tasks, report:\n\n```text\nBoundary Review: PASS / WARN / FAIL\nTouched boundaries:\nSource of truth:\nProjection surfaces:\nFindings:\nRequired fixes:\nRequired tests:\nAccepted debt, if any:\n```\n\nFor implementation tasks, keep this review internal while working, then summarize only the material findings and verification evidence.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\nA stateful change is not complete until:\n\n- The source-of-truth boundary is named and preserved.\n- Definition / instance / execution are not conflated.\n- External adapter results are converted to typed facts before routing.\n- Terminal states are guarded in core logic, not only UI/API.\n- Projection does not invent lifecycle state.\n- Current and historical semantics are separated.\n- Retry, repair, and compensation are distinct.\n- At least one boundary test or realistic check covers the risky transition.\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-23c4ac07-9eb9-417b-bbb1-055a33283992":{"tool_use_id":"exec-23c4ac07-9eb9-417b-bbb1-055a33283992","tool_name":"rtk read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.application;\\n\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.EvidenceStatus;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingHistoryEvidence;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingRatePoint;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessment;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessmentRequest;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.Recommendation;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.TerminalPolicy;\\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\\n\\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\\nimport java.math.MathContext;\\nimport java.time.Instant;\\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.Comparator;\\nimport java.util.List;\\nimport java.util.Optional;\\n\\n@Service\\npublic class PhaseOneAssessmentService {\\n\\n    private static final MathContext CALCULATION_CONTEXT = MathContext.DECIMAL128;\\n    private static final BigDecimal DAYS_PER_YEAR = new BigDecimal(\\\"365\\\");\\n    private static final BigDecimal MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL = new BigDecimal(\\\"5000\\\");\\n    private static final String EXCHANGE = \\\"OKX\\\";\\n    private static final String INSTRUMENT = \\\"BTC-USDT-SWAP\\\";\\n\\n    private final FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery;\\n\\n    public PhaseOneAssessmentService(FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery) {\\n        this.fundingRateFactQuery = fundingRateFactQuery;\\n    }\\n\\n    public PhaseOneAssessment assess(PhaseOneAssessmentRequest request) {\\n        List<FundingRatePoint> points = fundingRateFactQuery.findRealizedRates(\\n                EXCHANGE, INSTRUMENT, request.from(), request.to(), request.evaluationAsOf());\\n        List<FundingRatePoint> ordered = points.stream()\\n                .sorted(Comparator.comparing(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime))\\n                .toList();\\n\\n        BigDecimal holdingReturn = ordered.stream()\\n                .map(FundingRatePoint::realizedRate)\\n                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\\n        BigDecimal fundingIncome = request.hedgedShortNotional().multiply(holdingReturn);\\n        BigDecimal simpleEarnIncome = request.candidateCapital()\\n                .multiply(request.simpleEarnQuote().apr())\\n                .multiply(new BigDecimal(request.simpleEarnQuote().termDays()))\\n                .divide(DAYS_PER_YEAR, CALCULATION_CONTEXT);\\n        BigDecimal knownCost = request.costs().knownTotal();\\n\\n        FundingHistoryEvidence history = new FundingHistoryEvidence(\\n                holdingReturn,\\n                fundingIncome,\\n                ordered.size(),\\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() > 0).count(),\\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() < 0).count(),\\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).min(Instant::compareTo),\\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).max(Instant::compareTo));\\n\\n        List<String> blockers = new ArrayList<>();\\n        List<String> unknowns = new ArrayList<>(request.costs().unknowns());\\n        List<String> reasons = new ArrayList<>();\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> netIncome = Optional.empty();\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> incremental = Optional.empty();\\n        EvidenceStatus evidenceStatus;\\n        Recommendation recommendation;\\n\\n        if (!request.simpleEarnQuote().termsConfirmed()) {\\n            blockers.add(\\\"简单赚币确认页条款尚未人工确认\\\");\\n        }\\n        if (ordered.isEmpty()) {\\n            blockers.add(\\\"90 天窗口内没有可用的已实现资金费率事实\\\");\\n        }\\n        if (request.terminalPolicy() == TerminalPolicy.KEEP_STRATEGY_OPEN) {\\n            unknowns.add(\\\"期末未退出，无法与到期回到 USDT 的简单赚币同口径比较\\\");\\n        }\\n\\n        if (!blockers.isEmpty()) {\\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\\n            recommendation = Recommendation.INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE;\\n            reasons.addAll(blockers);\\n        } else if (!unknowns.isEmpty()) {\\n            evidenceStat..."},"output":{"formatted_output":"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.application;\n\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.EvidenceStatus;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingHistoryEvidence;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingRatePoint;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessment;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessmentRequest;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.Recommendation;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.TerminalPolicy;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.MathContext;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\n@Service\npublic class PhaseOneAssessmentService {\n\n    private static final MathContext CALCULATION_CONTEXT = MathContext.DECIMAL128;\n    private static final BigDecimal DAYS_PER_YEAR = new BigDecimal(\"365\");\n    private static final BigDecimal MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL = new BigDecimal(\"5000\");\n    private static final String EXCHANGE = \"OKX\";\n    private static final String INSTRUMENT = \"BTC-USDT-SWAP\";\n\n    private final FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery;\n\n    public PhaseOneAssessmentService(FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery) {\n        this.fundingRateFactQuery = fundingRateFactQuery;\n    }\n\n    public PhaseOneAssessment assess(PhaseOneAssessmentRequest request) {\n        List<FundingRatePoint> points = fundingRateFactQuery.findRealizedRates(\n                EXCHANGE, INSTRUMENT, request.from(), request.to(), request.evaluationAsOf());\n        List<FundingRatePoint> ordered = points.stream()\n                .sorted(Comparator.comparing(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime))\n                .toList();\n\n        BigDecimal holdingReturn = ordered.stream()\n                .map(FundingRatePoint::realizedRate)\n                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\n        BigDecimal fundingIncome = request.hedgedShortNotional().multiply(holdingReturn);\n        BigDecimal simpleEarnIncome = request.candidateCapital()\n                .multiply(request.simpleEarnQuote().apr())\n                .multiply(new BigDecimal(request.simpleEarnQuote().termDays()))\n                .divide(DAYS_PER_YEAR, CALCULATION_CONTEXT);\n        BigDecimal knownCost = request.costs().knownTotal();\n\n        FundingHistoryEvidence history = new FundingHistoryEvidence(\n                holdingReturn,\n                fundingIncome,\n                ordered.size(),\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() > 0).count(),\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() < 0).count(),\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).min(Instant::compareTo),\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).max(Instant::compareTo));\n\n        List<String> blockers = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<String> unknowns = new ArrayList<>(request.costs().unknowns());\n        List<String> reasons = new ArrayList<>();\n        Optional<BigDecimal> netIncome = Optional.empty();\n        Optional<BigDecimal> incremental = Optional.empty();\n        EvidenceStatus evidenceStatus;\n        Recommendation recommendation;\n\n        if (!request.simpleEarnQuote().termsConfirmed()) {\n            blockers.add(\"简单赚币确认页条款尚未人工确认\");\n        }\n        if (ordered.isEmpty()) {\n            blockers.add(\"90 天窗口内没有可用的已实现资金费率事实\");\n        }\n        if (request.terminalPolicy() == TerminalPolicy.KEEP_STRATEGY_OPEN) {\n            unknowns.add(\"期末未退出，无法与到期回到 USDT 的简单赚币同口径比较\");\n        }\n\n        if (!blockers.isEmpty()) {\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\n            recommendation = Recommendation.INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE;\n            reasons.addAll(blockers);\n        } else if (!unknowns.isEmpty()) {\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\n            recommendation = Recommendation.WATCH_SMART_ARBITRAGE;\n            reasons.add(\"关键成本或期末状态仍未知，不能把未知按 0 计算\");\n        } else {\n            BigDecimal net = fundingIncome.subtract(knownCost);\n            BigDecimal delta = net.subtract(simpleEarnIncome);\n            netIncome = Optional.of(net);\n            incremental = Optional.of(delta);\n            if (delta.signum() <= 0) {\n                evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.SUFFICIENT_FOR_COMPARISON;\n                recommendation = Recommendation.PREFER_SIMPLE_EARN;\n                reasons.add(\"资金费率收入扣除完整已知成本后不高于 90 天简单赚币\");\n            } else {\n                evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.SUFFICIENT_FOR_MICRO_VALIDATION;\n                recommendation = Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE;\n                reasons.add(\"历史情景扣除完整已知成本后高于简单赚币，但尚无真实闭环\");\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<String> checklist = recommendation == Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE\n                ? List.of(\n                        \"重新核对 OKX 90 天简单赚币 APR、额度和赎回条款\",\n                        \"重新打开 BTC-USDT 智能套利预览并核对两腿名义和预计开仓成本\",\n                        \"首次只投入 2,000–5,000 USDT\",\n                        \"保存实际成交、资金费、再平衡和退出费用\",\n                        \"退出回 USDT 后复盘预计与实际差异\")\n                : List.of();\n\n        return new PhaseOneAssessment(\n                request, simpleEarnIncome, history, knownCost, netIncome, incremental,\n                evidenceStatus, recommendation,\n                recommendation == Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE\n                        ? Optional.of(MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL) : Optional.empty(),\n                reasons, blockers, unknowns, checklist);\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-56195f78-def4-45b6-aed5-aa5238656141":{"tool_use_id":"exec-56195f78-def4-45b6-aed5-aa5238656141","tool_name":"rtk read .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/artifacts/contracts/node-contract-compile-007/task-contract.md","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"# Task Contract\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\n在既有 Java 项目 assess-income phase-one 的 90 天历史情景评估中新增可解释指标：在相同 90 天窗口、投入资金、对冲空头名义金额和固定已知成本口径下，资金费净收入追平简单赚币所需的整个 90 天累计资金费率阈值，由 PhaseOneAssessmentService 计算、PhaseOneAssessment record 承载、CLI 只读展示，并保留证据不足时的不可用语义。\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n**Excluded:**\\n- 不修改交易/账户、采集（sync-market/sync-product）、数据库迁移、持仓、调度、组合策略、Web 页面、Dual 生产代码或客户端配置\\n- 不接入任何新外部服务，不做未来费率预测或交易建议\\n- 不做整个项目的公式重构，不新增平台、规则 DSL 或兼容机制\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] AC-1: 计算口径：阈值 =（既有简单赚币 90 天收入 + 同口径完整已知成本）/ 对冲空头名义金额；该值是整个 90 天窗口的累计资金费率，不是 APR，不得按每次结算或假定 8 小时间隔换算；成本沿用 SmartArbitrageCosts.knownTotal() 既有口径，不重复计费；计算使用 BigDecimal 且精度规则明确（与既有服务的 DECIMAL128 计算上下文一致，除法精度显式声明）。\\n- [ ] AC-2: 独立样例与边界：共同资金 20,000 USDT、简单赚币 APR 0.0365、90 天、完整成本 20 USDT、对冲名义 10,000 USDT 时，对照收益为 180 USDT、阈值为 0.02（2%）；累计费率分别为 0.019、0.020、0.021 时，现有同口径增量分别为 -10、0、10 USDT；测试同时覆盖零已知成本、零 APR、负资金费率以及不能整除的精度场景；不得用舍入后的 CLI 数字重新决定现有建议。\\n- [ ] AC-3: 证据不足：只在现有评估允许同口径精确净收入比较时提供数值；成本缺失、简单赚币条款未确认、窗口内无历史结算或期末保持策略开放时数值不可用，并沿既有阻断项/未知项说明原因，不得填 0、猜数或给出可行动的精确阈值；非法或零名义金额沿 PhaseOneAssessmentRequest 既有输入校验拒绝（hedgedShortNotional 必须大于 0）。\\n- [ ] AC-4: 唯一生产与展示：现有评估服务产生 typed 结果（阈值作为 PhaseOneAssessment 的字段），CLI 只消费该结果，清楚标注“90 天累计资金费率阈值”及不可用情况，不自行重算；补充一份简明中文使用说明，包含上述样例和限制；既有建议、首次小额验证上限（5,000 USDT）、成本和风险语义不变。\\n- [ ] AC-5: 回归与交付：在固定隔离基线（当前分支 codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026 @ 7c5facc）上实现；相关服务/CLI 测试、既有非容器回归和 Gate 要求的完整基线回归保留并通过，执行测试有程序工具观察和报告依据（如 Maven Surefire 报告），不能只以模型“已通过”正文作数；独立验收完成后，仍需当前交付批准、精确候选应用、人工或另行明确委派的 commit、原 finalize，才能称完整 E2E 完成。\\n\\n## Test Requirements\\n\\n- TR-1: PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest 增加阈值单元测试：验证 AC-2 样例（对照收益 180 USDT、阈值 0.02）与累计费率 0.019/0.020/0.021 对应既有同口径增量 -10/0/+10 USDT，并覆盖零已知成本、零 APR、负资金费率和除不尽的精度场景；断言基于 BigDecimal 原值而非 CLI 舍入输出。\\n- TR-2: PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest 增加不可用与校验测试：成本缺失、条款未确认、无历史结算、期末保持策略开放时阈值为空且原因沿既有 blockers/unknowns 输出；非法或零对冲名义金额在读取事实前被既有请求校验拒绝。\\n- TR-3: AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest 增加展示测试：完整证据时输出含“90 天累计资金费率阈值”标签及数值，证据不足时输出不可用说明且不打印数值；既有建议文案、首次实盘上限、退出码与限制提示不回归。\\n- TR-4: 在固定隔离基线上运行既有非容器回归和 Gate 要求的完整基线回归（mvn 测试），以 Maven/Surefire 等程序工具生成的报告作为通过依据，并保留完整基线通过事实。\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- 继续使用现有 Java、BigDecimal、PhaseOneAssessmentService 评估服务和 assess-income CLI，不接入任何新外部服务或数据源。\\n- 阈值是整个 90 天窗口的累计资金费率，禁止换算成 APR 或按每次结算/假定 8 小时间隔折算；资金费间隔遵循实际 fundingTime。\\n- 成本口径沿用 SmartArbitrageCosts.knownTotal() 既有实现，不重复计费、不改变未知成本按 UNKNOWN 处理的语义；阈值的可用条件与既有增量比较的可用条件一致。\\n- 单一生产来源：阈值只在 PhaseOneAssessmentService 内计算并作为 typed 字段返回；CLI 是薄适配层，只打印该结果，不重算、不用舍入值影响建议。\\n- 资金费事实表、数据库迁移、同步/回补、组合策略与 Web 输出保持不动（只读）；新增说明文档为中文，沿用 docs 目录编号惯例。\\n- 精度规则显式：服务层计算与既有 CALCULATION_CONTEXT（MathContext.DECIMAL128）一致且除法上下文明确，展示层沿用 CLI 既有格式化惯例并标注为累计费率而非年化。\\n\\n## Non-Goals\\n\\n- 不做未来资金费率预测、完整套利收益保证或交易建议；阈值仅用于历史情景比较，既有未覆盖风险与历史完整性限制继续保留。\\n- 不修改交易/账户、采集、数据库迁移、持仓、调度、组合策略、Web 页面、Dual 生产代码或客户端配置。\\n- 不把收益阈值推广为整个项目的公式重构，不新增平台、规则 DSL 或兼容机制。\\n- 不改变既有建议逻辑、首次小额验证上限（5,000 USDT）、成本与风险/限制提示语义。\\n- 发现实现依赖超出上述范围（如需要改迁移、Web 或组合代码）时停止并提交取舍，不擅自扩大实现。\\n\\n## Risk Areas\\n\\n- 阈值展示格式（小数位/百分比）需要在设计评审确定，避免被误读为 APR 或单次费率；服务层核心值保持 DECIMAL128 不预先舍入。\\n- 为 PhaseOneAssessment record 新增字段会改变构造签名，当前构造点仅在 PhaseOneAssessmentService，需在执行时确认无其他调用点遗漏。\\n- 新说明文档建议命名 docs/15-Funding-Rate-Break-Even-Threshold.md（沿用 docs 01–14 编号惯例），最终路径以 EXECUTION 批准的精确 scope 为准。\\n\\n## Evidence References\\n\\n- src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java\\n- src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java\\n- src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessmentRequest.java\\n- src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/SmartArbitrageCosts.java\\n- src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java\\n- src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest.java\\n- src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest.java\\n- docs/09-Phase-1-Test-Runbook.md\\n\\n## Nonessential Operation Declarations\\n\\n- None\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n- **Created by:** contract.compile\\n- **Raw request:** .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/requirement.md\\n\\n\",\"exit_..."},"output":{"formatted_output":"# Task Contract\n\n## Objective\n\n在既有 Java 项目 assess-income phase-one 的 90 天历史情景评估中新增可解释指标：在相同 90 天窗口、投入资金、对冲空头名义金额和固定已知成本口径下，资金费净收入追平简单赚币所需的整个 90 天累计资金费率阈值，由 PhaseOneAssessmentService 计算、PhaseOneAssessment record 承载、CLI 只读展示，并保留证据不足时的不可用语义。\n\n## Scope\n\n**Excluded:**\n- 不修改交易/账户、采集（sync-market/sync-product）、数据库迁移、持仓、调度、组合策略、Web 页面、Dual 生产代码或客户端配置\n- 不接入任何新外部服务，不做未来费率预测或交易建议\n- 不做整个项目的公式重构，不新增平台、规则 DSL 或兼容机制\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC-1: 计算口径：阈值 =（既有简单赚币 90 天收入 + 同口径完整已知成本）/ 对冲空头名义金额；该值是整个 90 天窗口的累计资金费率，不是 APR，不得按每次结算或假定 8 小时间隔换算；成本沿用 SmartArbitrageCosts.knownTotal() 既有口径，不重复计费；计算使用 BigDecimal 且精度规则明确（与既有服务的 DECIMAL128 计算上下文一致，除法精度显式声明）。\n- [ ] AC-2: 独立样例与边界：共同资金 20,000 USDT、简单赚币 APR 0.0365、90 天、完整成本 20 USDT、对冲名义 10,000 USDT 时，对照收益为 180 USDT、阈值为 0.02（2%）；累计费率分别为 0.019、0.020、0.021 时，现有同口径增量分别为 -10、0、10 USDT；测试同时覆盖零已知成本、零 APR、负资金费率以及不能整除的精度场景；不得用舍入后的 CLI 数字重新决定现有建议。\n- [ ] AC-3: 证据不足：只在现有评估允许同口径精确净收入比较时提供数值；成本缺失、简单赚币条款未确认、窗口内无历史结算或期末保持策略开放时数值不可用，并沿既有阻断项/未知项说明原因，不得填 0、猜数或给出可行动的精确阈值；非法或零名义金额沿 PhaseOneAssessmentRequest 既有输入校验拒绝（hedgedShortNotional 必须大于 0）。\n- [ ] AC-4: 唯一生产与展示：现有评估服务产生 typed 结果（阈值作为 PhaseOneAssessment 的字段），CLI 只消费该结果，清楚标注“90 天累计资金费率阈值”及不可用情况，不自行重算；补充一份简明中文使用说明，包含上述样例和限制；既有建议、首次小额验证上限（5,000 USDT）、成本和风险语义不变。\n- [ ] AC-5: 回归与交付：在固定隔离基线（当前分支 codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026 @ 7c5facc）上实现；相关服务/CLI 测试、既有非容器回归和 Gate 要求的完整基线回归保留并通过，执行测试有程序工具观察和报告依据（如 Maven Surefire 报告），不能只以模型“已通过”正文作数；独立验收完成后，仍需当前交付批准、精确候选应用、人工或另行明确委派的 commit、原 finalize，才能称完整 E2E 完成。\n\n## Test Requirements\n\n- TR-1: PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest 增加阈值单元测试：验证 AC-2 样例（对照收益 180 USDT、阈值 0.02）与累计费率 0.019/0.020/0.021 对应既有同口径增量 -10/0/+10 USDT，并覆盖零已知成本、零 APR、负资金费率和除不尽的精度场景；断言基于 BigDecimal 原值而非 CLI 舍入输出。\n- TR-2: PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest 增加不可用与校验测试：成本缺失、条款未确认、无历史结算、期末保持策略开放时阈值为空且原因沿既有 blockers/unknowns 输出；非法或零对冲名义金额在读取事实前被既有请求校验拒绝。\n- TR-3: AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest 增加展示测试：完整证据时输出含“90 天累计资金费率阈值”标签及数值，证据不足时输出不可用说明且不打印数值；既有建议文案、首次实盘上限、退出码与限制提示不回归。\n- TR-4: 在固定隔离基线上运行既有非容器回归和 Gate 要求的完整基线回归（mvn 测试），以 Maven/Surefire 等程序工具生成的报告作为通过依据，并保留完整基线通过事实。\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 继续使用现有 Java、BigDecimal、PhaseOneAssessmentService 评估服务和 assess-income CLI，不接入任何新外部服务或数据源。\n- 阈值是整个 90 天窗口的累计资金费率，禁止换算成 APR 或按每次结算/假定 8 小时间隔折算；资金费间隔遵循实际 fundingTime。\n- 成本口径沿用 SmartArbitrageCosts.knownTotal() 既有实现，不重复计费、不改变未知成本按 UNKNOWN 处理的语义；阈值的可用条件与既有增量比较的可用条件一致。\n- 单一生产来源：阈值只在 PhaseOneAssessmentService 内计算并作为 typed 字段返回；CLI 是薄适配层，只打印该结果，不重算、不用舍入值影响建议。\n- 资金费事实表、数据库迁移、同步/回补、组合策略与 Web 输出保持不动（只读）；新增说明文档为中文，沿用 docs 目录编号惯例。\n- 精度规则显式：服务层计算与既有 CALCULATION_CONTEXT（MathContext.DECIMAL128）一致且除法上下文明确，展示层沿用 CLI 既有格式化惯例并标注为累计费率而非年化。\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- 不做未来资金费率预测、完整套利收益保证或交易建议；阈值仅用于历史情景比较，既有未覆盖风险与历史完整性限制继续保留。\n- 不修改交易/账户、采集、数据库迁移、持仓、调度、组合策略、Web 页面、Dual 生产代码或客户端配置。\n- 不把收益阈值推广为整个项目的公式重构，不新增平台、规则 DSL 或兼容机制。\n- 不改变既有建议逻辑、首次小额验证上限（5,000 USDT）、成本与风险/限制提示语义。\n- 发现实现依赖超出上述范围（如需要改迁移、Web 或组合代码）时停止并提交取